      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hopefully a blink toggle doesn't mess with blinking controlled by the tracking component for SDK3 avatars.\nWhen the camera is out and an avatar is within range (or looking directly at the camera), the game should ignore whats set with the tracking component and disable blinking.\nIt should not disable or enable blinking directly on the avatars tracking component to prevent issues with 3.0 logic handling blinking.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-13T22:06:29.365Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A togglable option to allow avatars Eye-tracking to fixate on the lens. So for example, when I take a picture with a friend, their eyes are fixated on the camera instead of me. Since Eye tracking is local, it seemed plausible. \nAlso a \"blink\" prevention toggle could be useful to prevent users from blinking while the camera is in use, unless the player is using a gesture.",
